      "body_html": "HOLY GUACAMOLE!  Another white lipped clone, here's the first one that has ever been documented, it's from franklin Co, FL : <a href=\"https://sarracenia.proboards.com/thread/3753/leucophylla-red-white-lips-franklin\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">sarracenia.proboards.com/thread/3753/leucophylla-red-white-lips-franklin</a> <br/><br/><br/>The added bonus to this plant is the solid red body, which really makes  the thick, white lips bling out in this clone!  This is still a seedling, so we'll see what happens when it gets bigger.  Pretty cool, eh?  we'll see if I can get em lips whiter, I bet it's very environmentally induced.      Pics taken 5/6/20:<br/><br/><br/><img src=\"https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/49867760252_7df5b6f283_c.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/><img src=\"https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/49866910423_78dc68bdfa_c.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/><img src=\"https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/49867444756_f59fbc29d8_c.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/>",
